Ubuntu package builds for ONNX Runtime
======================================

This directory is an Ubuntu-oriented package recipe for the CPU shared library
and development files. It is intentionally smaller than Debian's package: it
does not build the Python bindings, tools, or optional execution providers.

Unlike Debian's archive package, this recipe lets ONNX Runtime's CMake project
fetch and statically link its pinned third-party dependencies. This avoids
backporting a large dependency stack to older Ubuntu releases, but it also means
the build requires network access and is not suitable for Debian or Ubuntu's
network-isolated official package builders. ThirdPartyNotices.txt is shipped in
the runtime package for the bundled dependency notices.

The GitHub Actions workflow builds in a container matching the target release.
In particular, the Ubuntu 20.04 binary must not be built directly on a 22.04
host: doing so can introduce glibc and libstdc++ symbol requirements that are
not present on 20.04. Ubuntu 20.04 uses ONNX Runtime 1.21.1, the final practical
release line for its stock GCC 9 toolchain. Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 use 1.27.1.
The Focal build also applies `focal-eigen-download.patch`: it keeps 1.21.1's
exact Eigen commit but moves the download to Eigen's GitHub mirror because the
bytes generated by the original GitLab archive URL no longer match the hash
pinned by that release.

Debian's complete packaging metadata can be downloaded without its repacked
upstream source by fetching the debian.tar.xz member of the source package:

  curl -LO https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/o/onnxruntime/onnxruntime_1.27.1+dfsg-1.debian.tar.xz
  tar -xf onnxruntime_1.27.1+dfsg-1.debian.tar.xz

Use `dget` on the matching `.dsc` instead when the complete, checksummed Debian
source package is required.
